# sm112, the crumb-pocket hive hand (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 2: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle sm112
revision 2
state ready
dialect southmeadow
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for cty_disa_fogford
written_by claude
title the crumb-pocket hive hand
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=farmer talk=quiet
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk feeds_the_sparrows
likes honey_cakes roof_birds quiet_chapel thunder
dislikes haggling crowds
fears losing_the_roof_over_us going_back_to_nothing
hopes a_winter_with_the_larder_never_bare to_keep_what_was_built
topics animals +0.4 work +0.3 weather +0.3 home +0.2 faith +0.2 festival -0.3 gossip -0.2
styles comfort=quiet gossip=reluctant refuse=short tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# works the hives for a keeper's wage, keeps an apron pocket full of crumbs for the sparrows on the shed roof, says little and says it dry, and is quietly proud of every stick that was earned from nothing.

words
oath! = Crumbs and comb | By the thunder and the thatch
saying! = A full sparrow leaves the bees be | Nothing's a fine place to start from | Thunder's only the sky clearing its throat
sparrows = the sparrows | my little thieves on the shed roof
crumbs = crumbs | a pocket of crumbs
cake = a honey cake | honey cakes still warm off the griddle
storm = a thunderstorm | a good loud storm
roof = a sound roof | a roof that keeps the wet out
shed = the hive shed | the shed
hives = the hives | the long row of hives
haggle = haggling | squabbling over a penny
press = a crowd | a press of folk
nothing = nothing but my paws | two paws and an empty sack
pocket = my apron pocket | my pinny pocket
stillchapel = the chapel on a weekday | a chapel with only me and the dust in it
crooked = the one with the crooked tail | old crooked-tail

any
opinion @1 city against 1 : The city's elbows and smoke. Nobody there would know your face if you fell down in the street, #address#.
opinion @1 festivals against 1 : I'll watch the feast from my own step. #press.capitalize# isn't my idea of a good time.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : I've worked under the Houses since I was a #child#, and never set eyes on one of them.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : They price a loaf like it's gold, and then they want you to #haggle# for it. I'll pay or I'll walk.
opinion @1 newcomers mixed 1 : There's little enough work. Still, everybody starts from nothing somewhere. I'd not grudge them the start.
opinion @1 times against 1 : The #wages# stay where they are and the bread climbs. And the ones who could mend it never look down.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Mind the hives; stand still if one comes near. | #greet#. You're not from the lane, I'd say.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=farmer] : #greet#. I'm in among #hives#. Shout if you need me. | #greet#. Keep your voice down; #hives# are in a temper.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. #sparrows.capitalize# are up. So am I. | #greet#. Early. The crumbs go out first.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Late for wandering, #address#. | #greet#. The day's #tired#, and so am I.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Oh, it's you. Sit. There's #cake# going. | You'll be #hungry#. Sit down.
line @1 again.open : You again. #welcome_back#. | Twice. I'll put a crumb out for you.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. Well enough.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. Good, it's you. | #greet#. Sit down; you look #tired#.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Busy, but talk on. | #greet#. Mind the bees.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Late, but come in. | #greet#. The lamp's still lit.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Keep clear of the hive fronts.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #s8_night#. | #farewell#. Keep under a roof, it looks like thunder.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #s8_byeback#.
line @1 react.news : #ack#. | #surprise#. There's a thing.
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#. Not heard that. | #oath#. That's new to me, #address#.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. | Old chaff. The sparrows had it first.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. Let a second mouth say it, then I'll listen. | #demur#. I'll hold off believing it.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. | That's a #bad# business. I'm sorry for it.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. | #good.capitalize#. There's honey cake in that, somewhere.
line @1 answer.how : #fine#. | #tired.capitalize#, but upright. | Fair. Stung twice, fed #sparrows#, still here.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#. The bees don't stop for me. | Up to my elbows in #hives#.
line @1 ask.how : And you? | Keeping dry, #address#?
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. | That's #bad#. Sit with me a bit.
line @1 decline : #hedge#, but no. The hives want me, and they don't wait. | Not today, #address#. I've #work# to finish and I'm #tired# already.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. | Fair. Another day.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. | Kind of you. I'll owe you #cake#.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect#. | Nothing. Leave it at that.
line @1 preclose : Well. #preclose#. | The bees are calling, #address#.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then. | #s8_okay#.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : There's drowned sparrows look happier than you. | You walk like you're carrying #shed# on your back.
line @1 tease.return : #cheek#. | Sharp as a sickle, that tongue.
line @1 ack : #ack#. | #bc_it_is#
rule @crumbs
when concept=bark self.likes=roof_birds working=no
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There you are. #crumbs.capitalize#, and no squabbling. | Here, #crooked#. You first.

rule @bees
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=farmer
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Easy now. Nobody's robbing #hives# today. | #oath#. One's up my sleeve again.

rule @thunder
when concept=bark here.weather=storm self.likes=thunder
does aside
cooldown 12h
say Hark at that. #saying.capitalize#. | #storm.capitalize#. Lovely, from under #roof#.

rule @haggle
when concept=bark here.place=market self.dislikes=haggling
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Pay it or leave it. Don't squabble at me. | #haggle.capitalize#. #annoyed#.

scene sparrow_crumbs
when topic=animals self.likes=roof_birds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I feed #sparrows# every morning. Folk say it's daft for a hive hand. | #pocket.capitalize#'s full of crumbs for the sparrows. Always is. | #sparrows.capitalize# wait for me. Seven of them, most days.
b : Why daft? | Always? | Only seven?
a : Sparrows eat bees. I fill them up with #crumbs# so they've no room left. | Always. I've gone without breakfast before I've let them. | Seven regulars. The rest are only passing through, #address#.
b : #bc_clever# | #bc_poor_soul# | Ha.

scene sparrow_names
when topic=smalltalk|animals self.likes=roof_birds
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I can tell every one of #sparrows# apart. There's #crooked#, and the bold one, and the one that sulks. | #crooked.capitalize# took a crumb from my paw today. Took a year to get that far. | A cat had a go at #sparrows# last week. I had a go at the cat.
b : They all look the same to me. | A whole year? | Who won?
a : They would. You've not looked properly. #bc_i_know# | A year. I'm #slow#, and so are they. We suit. | The sparrows. The cat's not been back.

scene roof_watch
when topic=pastimes self.likes=roof_birds
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Restdays, I'm on my step with my eyes up on the roof ridges. That's my pastime. | A starling on the chapel roof was mocking the bell this morning. Near enough. | I watch the rooftops. Every roof's got its own birds, and its own quarrels, #address#.
b : That's restful. | Mocking the bell? | Like the street below.
a : It is. Nobody asks me for anything up there. | Bong, bong, it went. Then it fell off. #bc_ha# | Same squabbles. Less shouting. #very.capitalize# restful.

scene thunder_roof
when topic=weather here.weather=storm self.likes=thunder
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Listen to that. I could sit through a storm all night, under #roof#. | #storm.capitalize#. The bees hate it. I don't mind it at all. | #storm.capitalize#. I open the shutters a crack to hear it better.
b : It scares me. | Why don't you mind? | Doesn't the rain come in?
a : It's only the sky clearing its throat, #address#. | I've #roof# over me. That's all that matters. | A bit. That's the price of a good #storm#.

scene rain_shed
when topic=weather|work here.weather=rain self.job=farmer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #rain.capitalize#. The bees won't fly, so I'm mending frames in the shed. | Wet day. #hives.capitalize# are quiet and so am I. | Rain on #shed# roof. Best sound there is, after thunder.
b : A quiet day, then. | Suits you. | You like the rain?
a : Quiet and dry. I'll take it. | It does. I've no complaints today, #address#. | From under #roof#, yes. Out in it, no.

scene honey_cake
when topic=food self.likes=honey_cakes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #cake.capitalize#. I've walked a mile for one before now. | I make #cake# on Restday. Half for us, half for the sparrows. | Honey from our hives, flour from the mill. That's a cake with no #stranger# in it.
b : A mile? | Half for the birds? | That's a good cake.
a : Uphill. In the rain. It was worth it, #address#. | They earn it. They keep #hives# safe, in a way. | #good.capitalize#. And I made it with my own paws.

scene hive_day
when topic=work self.job=farmer self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I lift what I'm told to and watch what I'm not. #hives.capitalize# teach the rest. | Twelve hives before noon. I count #hives# so I don't miss one. | Got stung on the nose this morning. #oath#. It's still #hurt#.
b : What do you watch? | All twelve? | On the nose?
a : The bees. They'll tell you when something's wrong, if you're quiet enough. | All twelve. Then the next twelve. #bc_every_day# | The nose. I've a nose like a plum now. #bc_ha#

scene from_nothing
when topic=memories|work self.age>=30
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I started with #nothing#. I'll not pretend otherwise. | Everything I've got, I earned a penny at a time. It's #little#, but it's all mine. | Nobody handed me a thing. I'm quietly proud of that.
b : That's something to be proud of. | Mine too. | You should be.
a : I'm not loud about it. #nothing.capitalize# keeps you quiet. | Then you know. It's a #good# feeling, isn't it. | I am. Quietly, mind. #bc_it_is#

scene our_roof
when topic=home self.married=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : We've #roof# and a fire and a door that shuts. I never thought I'd say that. | My #self.spouse_word# and I put that home together a stick at a time. | It's a small place. But nobody can put us out of it, #address#.
b : That's plenty. | That's the way to do it. | That's what matters.
a : It's more than plenty. It's ours. | Slow, but it stays up. #saying.capitalize#. | It is. I check the latch on #roof# twice every night.

scene with_spouse
when topic=family|friends self.married=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.spouse# is the best thing I've ever got without paying for it. | I don't say much. My #self.spouse_word# doesn't need me to. | #self.spouse# knows me better than the sparrows do. And that's saying something.
b : That's lovely. | Good match, then. | That's high praise.
a : Don't tell anyone I said it. #bc_ha# | #bc_it_is# The best I could have made. | It's the highest I give, #address#.

scene haggling
when topic=prices|work self.dislikes=haggling
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : A buyer stood at the shed for an hour, #haggle#. Over honey. | I'll not haggle. Tell me the price, and I'll pay it or I'll leave. | Haggling's a game for folk with time. I've #hives#.
b : Some folk enjoy it. | That's honest. | It's how trade's done.
a : Some folk enjoy being stung too. Not many. | Honest's quicker. Nobody keeps a tally of lies. | Then I'll do less trade. #bad.capitalize# for me, but there it is.

scene crowds_edge
when topic=festival self.dislikes=crowds
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I watch the feast from my own step, away from #press#. | #press.capitalize# makes my fur prickle. I'll go when it's thinned out. | Festival day. #sparrows.capitalize# and I will keep the lane quiet.
b : You'll miss the fun. | It does get packed. | Fair enough.
a : I'll miss being trodden on. The fun I can hear. | Packed as a hive at swarming. #bc_i_know# | They're good company, the sparrows. They don't push.

scene still_chapel
when topic=faith self.likes=quiet_chapel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like #stillchapel#. There's sparrows in the rafters, and they sing better than the choir. | I slip in when it's empty. Prayers go better without an audience. | Empty chapel, dusty light, and nobody asking for a coin. That's my sort of prayer.
b : Sparrows in the chapel? | Fair enough. | It's peaceful.
a : Under the eaves. The priest doesn't know. Don't tell, #address#. | Fair, and quiet. That's all I want of it. | It is. Then the doors open and it's #nonsense# again.

scene lean_weeks
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : Lean weeks. The crumbs are smaller and #sparrows# have noticed. | Bread's dear and the #wages# aren't. We're managing. Just. | Thin times. I've been at #nothing# before; I know the way back if I must.
b : They'll manage. | You'll get by. | Let's hope not.
a : They will. Sparrows always do. #saying.capitalize#. | We will. #reassure#. | Let's. I'd rather not walk it twice.

scene gossip_aside
when topic=gossip
does tell.gossip / react.news / assess
a : I hear #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's all, and I'll say no more. | They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'd only tell the sparrows, usually. | Word is #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Not my business, #address#.
b : Is it true? | They'd keep it quiet. | Fair enough.
a : Couldn't tell you. #hearsay.capitalize#. | They would. Best listeners I know. | Suits me, that. #bc_it_is#

scene newcomer_start
when topic=newcomer
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : Somebody new in the lanes. They'll find #work#'s thin. | A newcomer's got #nothing# to start with, I expect. That's how most of us began. | New face at the gate. Time will show me what they're made of.
b : Work is thin. | You started that way? | Wise.
a : It is. Still, everybody needs a first penny, #address#. | Started with less. I'd not grudge anyone the same start. | Wise or #slow#. Sometimes the same thing.

scene winter_crumbs
when topic=season|animals here.season=winter self.likes=roof_birds
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : Winter's hard on #sparrows#. I double the crumbs when it's #cold#. | Found one frozen on the shed step this morning. I'll put more #crumbs# out. | The sparrows fluff up like little balls in the frost. They look like they're sulking.
b : They'll be all right. | That's a shame. | Maybe they are.
a : Most will. Not all. I do what I can. | It is. Not every one makes it. More crumbs tomorrow. | Likely. I would be, out there.

scene summer_swarm
when topic=work|season here.season=summer self.job=farmer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A swarm went over the shed today like smoke. I stood very still. | Summer's busy. The bees are fat and cross and so am I. | I caught a swarm in a basket this morning. My first this year, #oath#.
b : Did it settle? | Fat and cross? | Well done.
a : On the chapel roof. Somebody else's problem now. #bc_ha# | Full of honey and spoiling for a fight. #very.capitalize# busy, the lot of us. | Thank you. I didn't drop it, which is a first.

scene dusk_step
when topic=day here.time=dusk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Dusk. Me on the step, and #sparrows# going to roost one by one. | The day's done. I've #nothing# left in my paws, and that's how it should be. | This is the only hour I'm not working or sleeping, #address#.
b : Sounds peaceful. | Well earned. | Make the most of it.
a : It is. Then the cat comes and spoils it. | I'll take that. Every day of it. | I do. Then I'm asleep on the step, #tired#, most nights.

story first_crumb [topic=memories|animals self.age>=25]
  : As a #child# I had one crust for the day, and a sparrow sat on my paw and looked at it.
  : I gave it half. It came back the next day, and the next. That's where it started.
  ask : Have you ever had a creature follow you about like that?
  b : Once. A cat that thought it owned me.
  b[old] : A goat. For years. I never asked it to.

story empty_sack [topic=memories|work self.age>=30]
  : I started with #nothing#. One coat, one sack, and the sack was empty.
  : My first coin bought #cake#. I sat on a wall and shared it with three sparrows.
  : That was the best meal I've ever had, and I've had a few since.
  b : That's a good start. What happened to the coat?
  : Patched so often there's none of the first coat left in it. I still wear it.

story shed_storm [topic=weather|work self.job=farmer]
  : I was caught in the hive shed once when a storm came over. Thunder right on top of us.
  : The bees inside hummed louder and louder, like they were singing it down.
  : When it stopped they went quiet, all at once. I clapped. I don't know why.
  b : Ha. Did they mind?
  : Not a sting. I think they took it as their due.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. What is it? | #greet#. Mind the bees, and say your piece.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. Back again. | #topic.player#. #greet#. Crumbs, or conversation?
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=farmer] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I lift, carry and watch, and #hives# do the clever part. | Hives, frames, swarms, stings. And #sparrows#, but nobody pays me for those.
dlg @2 resident.job : #job_busy# | This and that. Mostly that.
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# | Nothing. Even #sparrows# are quiet.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | I don't carry tales. I've #crumbs# to carry.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Go round the hives, not past the front.
graft resident.hub
choice Why do you feed the sparrows? -> sparrows
node sparrows
say Sparrows eat bees. I fill them up with crumbs so they've no room left for mine. That's the reason I give, anyway.
mood calm
free
choice And the real reason? -> real
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node real
say A sparrow sat with me once when I had nothing else. I've been paying it back since, one crumb at a time.
choice That's kind. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
